| sp | 4 |
| depends_on | M1 |
| status | pending |

**Goal:** `shelfnet-crawler` owns a Postgres (`crawler-db`) holding its seen list and a `(provider, edition_id)`
edition cache, replacing the Redis seen hash.

**Scope:** `docker-compose.yml` (`crawler-db` service, `crawler-db-data` volume, `CRAWLER_DATABASE_URL`),
`.env.example`, `services/shelfnet-crawler/pyproject.toml` (`psycopg[binary]>=3.2`, already locked at 3.3.5),
new `shelfnet_crawler/db.py`, `shelfnet_crawler/edition.py` (`Edition`, `EditionCache`), re-backed `seen.py`,
`settings.py`, `main.py:run` wiring, `discovery.py` (type only), specs. Tables (crawler DB):
`edition(provider text, edition_id int, work_id int null, author text null, publisher text null, binding text null,
format text null, audience text null, height_cm real null, page_count int null, fetched_at timestamptz,
PRIMARY KEY (provider, edition_id))`; `seen(provider text, listing_id bigint, first_seen_at timestamptz,
PRIMARY KEY (provider, listing_id))`. Rollback: `docker compose rm -sf crawler-db && docker volume rm
<project>_crawler-db-data` — both tables are rebuildable.

#### Tasks

| Task | Description | Files | SP | Status |
|------|-------------|-------|----|--------|
| 6.1 | `crawler-db` service: `postgres:18`, user/password/db `crawler`, host port `${CRAWLER_DB_PORT:-4156}:5432`, healthcheck `pg_isready -U crawler`, volume `crawler-db-data`; `CRAWLER_DATABASE_URL: ${CRAWLER_DATABASE_URL:-postgres://crawler:crawler@crawler-db:5432/crawler}` in `x-service.environment`; `shelfnet-crawler` `depends_on` `crawler-db` healthy; append `CRAWLER_DATABASE_URL=postgres://crawler:crawler@localhost:4156/crawler` to `.env.example` | `docker-compose.yml`, `.env.example` | 1 | pending |
| 6.2 | `db.py`: `connect(url) -> AsyncConnection` (autocommit) and idempotent `ensure_schema(conn)`; `Settings.crawler_database_url` default `postgres://crawler:crawler@localhost:4156/crawler`; add `psycopg[binary]` dependency | `services/shelfnet-crawler/src/shelfnet_crawler/db.py`, `services/shelfnet-crawler/src/shelfnet_crawler/db_spec.py`, `services/shelfnet-crawler/src/shelfnet_crawler/settings.py`, `services/shelfnet-crawler/pyproject.toml`, `uv.lock` | 1 | pending |
| 6.3 | `SeenStore(conn, provider)` with unchanged `is_seen` / `mark` / `prune` signatures over table `seen` (`mark` = `INSERT … ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING`); drop `shelfnet_seen_key` setting; `run()` opens the connection, calls `ensure_schema`, closes in `finally` | `services/shelfnet-crawler/src/shelfnet_crawler/seen.py`, `services/shelfnet-crawler/src/shelfnet_crawler/seen_spec.py`, `services/shelfnet-crawler/src/shelfnet_crawler/settings.py`, `services/shelfnet-crawler/src/shelfnet_crawler/main.py`, `services/shelfnet-crawler/src/shelfnet_crawler/main_spec.py` | 1 | pending |
| 6.4 | `Edition` frozen dataclass + `EditionCache(conn, provider)` with `get(edition_id)` and `upsert(edition)` (`ON CONFLICT (provider, edition_id) DO UPDATE`, last-writer-wins) | `services/shelfnet-crawler/src/shelfnet_crawler/edition.py`, `services/shelfnet-crawler/src/shelfnet_crawler/edition_spec.py` | 1 | pending |

