## Final Verification

- [ ] `just up` then `docker compose ps` shows `crawler-db`, `api`, `api-consumer`, `record-processor`, `shelfnet-crawler` running/healthy.
- [ ] `just e2e` passes (player → record-processor → api; `Record.provider_id == "player"`, cover objects exist in rustfs).
- [ ] Live acceptance: with a rule `provider=shelfnet, max {"loan_count": 500}` created in `/admin/catalog/rule/`, `uv run python -m shelfnet_crawler --once --dry-run` logs `skip … rule=<id>` for every listing over 500 loans and `would publish` only for listings at or under it; the crawler log shows a 304 (or no request) on a second cycle inside 10 minutes.
- [ ] `just test` — all specs pass with `docker compose up -d redis postgres rustfs crawler-db` running (no skips from missing services).
- [ ] `just lint` and `just typecheck` — clean.
- [ ] `uv run python -m api makemigrations --check --dry-run` — no pending migrations.
- [ ] `uv run python -m event_schemas packages/event-schemas/schemas && git diff --exit-code packages/event-schemas/schemas` — schemas match models.
- [ ] `cd web && npm run lint` — clean.
- [ ] `uv run python -m api migrate catalog 0001 && uv run python -m api migrate` round-trips on a database holding e2e rows.

## Testing Strategy

Filtering and edition mapping run over real, messy provider data (label vocabularies, unit strings), so
correctness is partly empirical.

1. **Business-goal acceptance** — an admin-created rule removes exactly the intended inventory: after
   one live `--once` cycle with a loan-count or height rule, every `Record` row in `/admin/catalog/record/`
   created in that cycle satisfies the rule, and every skip log names the rule. Edition fields
   (`binding`, `format`, `height_cm`) are non-null on ≥ 80 % of records whose item page carried the
   corresponding key per the M7 recon table.
2. **Fast debug loop** — fixtures `services/shelfnet-crawler/src/shelfnet_crawler/fixtures/search_item.json`
   and `fixtures/getiteminfo.json`; `uv run pytest -q services/shelfnet-crawler/src/shelfnet_crawler/record_filter_spec.py
   services/shelfnet-crawler/src/shelfnet_crawler/normalize_spec.py` — pure functions, no services, < 2 s.
   New label variants found live are added as parametrised cases in `normalize_spec.py`.
3. **User-facing validation** — `uv run python -m shelfnet_crawler --once --dry-run` (prints per-listing
   `skip …` / `would publish …` without touching the stream or the seen list) lets the admin preview a
   rule before activating it; the Django admin `Rule` changelist (`list_editable` `active`) and the SPA
   detail "Edition" section show the outcome.

