# M09: RecordFilter and the tiered crawl funnel

## Tasks

**Goal:** each cycle drops records at the cheapest tier that can decide — SERP, then cached edition, then
item page — logs every skip with its rule and reason, and publishes only fully compiled records.

**Scope:** new `services/shelfnet-crawler/src/shelfnet_crawler/record_filter.py` (+ spec), delete
`shelfnet_crawler/filters.py` and `filters_spec.py` (their cases move into `record_filter_spec.py`),
`main.py:_cycle` / `run` / `main` (rules refresh, edition resolution, `--dry-run`), `main_spec.py`.
Uses `SeenStore`, `Edition`, `EditionCache` (M6), `edition_from_detail`, `search_item_to_raw_record` (M7),
`RulesClient` (M8), `Rule` (M1).

| Task | Description | Files | SP | Status |
|------|-------------|-------|----|--------|
| 9.1 | `RecordFilter.pre_filter(item, edition=None)`: age on SERP year (`< cutoff.year` → DROP; equal/unparsable → deferred); per rule in scope (`work_id`/`edition_id` vs item `workid`/`editionid`): empty bounds → DROP; field values from SERP (`year`, `price`, `loan_count`, `height_cm` via `height`) else edition (`height_cm`, `page_count`); any violated bound → DROP with that rule; a bound needing the edition with `edition is None` → NEED_EDITION; unresolvable value → bound ignored; never returns NEED_EDITION when `edition` is given | `services/shelfnet-crawler/src/shelfnet_crawler/record_filter.py`, `services/shelfnet-crawler/src/shelfnet_crawler/record_filter_spec.py` | 2 | pending |
| 9.2 | `RecordFilter.post_filter(record: RawRecord)`: month cutoff for the boundary year (`acquired is None` → DROP "no usable acquireddate"; `< cutoff` → DROP); move `Cutoff`/`cutoff_for` into `record_filter.py`; delete `filters.py` + `filters_spec.py` with their cases ported | `services/shelfnet-crawler/src/shelfnet_crawler/record_filter.py`, `services/shelfnet-crawler/src/shelfnet_crawler/record_filter_spec.py`, `services/shelfnet-crawler/src/shelfnet_crawler/filters.py`, `services/shelfnet-crawler/src/shelfnet_crawler/filters_spec.py` | 1 | pending |
| 9.3 | Rewire `_cycle`: `rules.refresh_if_due()` → `RecordFilter(rules.rules, cutoff)` → per item `pre_filter`; NEED_EDITION → `EditionCache.get(editionid)` else fetch the item page + `edition_from_detail` + `upsert`, then `pre_filter(item, edition)`; item page (reuse if already fetched; `ShelfnetApiError` → warning, not marked, continue); `upsert` edition from every item page; map; `post_filter`; publish; mark. Every DROP → `logger.info("skip %s: rule=%s reason=%s", itemid, rule_id, reason)` + mark. `run()` owns `RulesClient`; `agerange` param unchanged | `services/shelfnet-crawler/src/shelfnet_crawler/main.py`, `services/shelfnet-crawler/src/shelfnet_crawler/main_spec.py` | 2 | pending |
| 9.4 | `--dry-run` flag: full funnel incl. item page and edition cache writes, logs `would publish <itemid>` instead of publishing, never calls `SeenStore.mark` | `services/shelfnet-crawler/src/shelfnet_crawler/main.py`, `services/shelfnet-crawler/src/shelfnet_crawler/main_spec.py` | 1 | pending |

## Definition of Done

##### Task 9.1
- [ ] `record_filter_spec.py` (pure, no I/O) parametrised over `search_item.json`: rule `max {"loan_count": 1000}` on an item with `loans "18"` (1 800 loans) → DROP with that rule id; `min {"height_cm": 30.0}` with `height "24cm"` → DROP; `min {"page_count": 200}` and `edition=None` → NEED_EDITION; same with `Edition(page_count=250)` → PASS; with `Edition(page_count=None)` → PASS (fail open).
- [ ] Scope: rule `work_id=110, edition_id=None, min={}, max={}` → DROP; `work_id=999` → PASS; `work_id=110, edition_id=1` on `editionid 2226` → PASS.
- [ ] Unparsable SERP `loans` (`"k. A."`) with a loan-count rule → PASS.
- [ ] Sketch:
  ```python
  class Action(StrEnum):
      DROP = "drop"; NEED_EDITION = "need_edition"; PASS = "pass"

  @dataclass(frozen=True)
  class Verdict:
      action: Action
      reason: str = ""
      rule_id: int | None = None

  class RecordFilter:
      def __init__(self, rules: Sequence[Rule], cutoff: Cutoff | None) -> None: ...
      def pre_filter(self, item: dict[str, Any], edition: Edition | None = None) -> Verdict: ...
      def post_filter(self, record: RawRecord) -> Verdict: ...
  ```

